# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Validated at boot by src/lib/env.ts. A missing or malformed value stops the app
# with a readable message rather than failing later at the first query.
#
# Supabase > Settings > API Keys issues two keys, and they are not interchangeable:
#   sb_publishable_...  safe in the browser. What RLS policies are written against.
#   sb_secret_...       bypasses EVERY RLS policy. Server-side only. Never ship it.
#
# If a key begins with "eyJ..." it is a legacy anon / service_role JWT. Supabase is
# retiring those by the end of 2026, so env.ts rejects them on purpose.

# Project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Publishable key. Exposed to the browser, protected by RLS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Absolute URL of this app. Used to build auth redirect links, so it must match a
# redirect URL registered in Supabase > Authentication > URL Configuration, or
# confirmation links will bounce to localhost. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Not read by the app. Only the Supabase CLI needs it, to apply migrations
# (`supabase link` / `supabase db push`). Put it in .env.local if you want the CLI
# to pick it up from there.
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=
